                <pb facs="1006" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg812"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/7–2345:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 877<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Director of the Office of Financial
                        and Development Policy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Collado</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Deputy to the Assistant Secretary of State for
                        Economic Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thorp</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">and the Acting Chief of the Division of Financial
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Reinstein</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d877-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, [<date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-23">July 23, 1945</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 215. For Thorp and Reinstein from
                    Collado. Present thought is that four power joint programming of imports,
                    exports and reparations and combined procurement and interim financing of
                    imports will not be feasible. We are consequently drafting on a zonal basis with
                    expectation of combined handling and financing for the three western zones. We
                    are preparing with McCloy and Hilldring a draft directive to War Department on
                    financing responsibility<anchor n="2" xml:id="d877-f2"/> along lines discussed
                    in Washington.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d877-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d877-f1-content">
